this is the amber platform project - a culture-first job matching platform.

code style:
- use lowercase for all ui text
- prefer functional components in react
- use type hints in python
- write clear, self-documenting code
- add comments for complex logic

architecture:
- frontend: react 19 + typescript + vite
- styling: tailwind css with amber design system
- backend: python + fastapi
- database: supabase (postgresql + auth + storage)
- state: react context + zustand

when writing code:
- follow the component patterns in src/frontend/src/components/ui/
- use css variables for theming (see globals.css)
- implement role-based access (candidate vs employer)
- write type-safe code with typescript
- keep functions small and focused

design system:
- primary accent: amber-600 (#D97706)
- muted text: stone-500 (#78716C)
- background: cream-100 (#F5F3EF)
- always use css variables for colors
- follow the Button, Input, Card patterns

project values:
- culture-first matching (personality + values)
- beautiful, accessible ui
- type safety throughout
- privacy conscious (rls policies)
- simplicity (lowercase aesthetic, minimal ui)
